- Story & Context: Months after the dynasties fractured into scattered road crews, local harbor divers still claimed that whenever the neap tide receded past the slipway, the mud itself hummed with sub-bass and the phantom metallic chime of a cracked ride cymbal. Siobhan recorded the aftermath with an ambient field mic strapped to a dead cormorant decoy, capturing the eerie hiss of the receding Atlantic over her own overdriven guitar feedback and Lyle’s ghost-like, spoken-word epilogue. The track ends on a dying loop of the wedding crowd’s distant, drunken sobbing beneath the final hook: "We left the wedding rings to tarnish in the soundman's mud."
